A day number before an English month gives a large negative response. A
quantity before an East Asian counting unit gives a positive response, strongest
for years, weeks and repetitions. Calendar years are much weaker than short
counts. Joined numeral/unit tokens are handled too. All other predictions are
zero, except for 'int main', numeric operators, and a split 'au' vowel
sequence ending in a nasal consonant.
