"""A negative pulse at document starts, sustained by an identical-token run.

The pulse is stronger for words than punctuation, and especially strong for
unspaced capitalized words. Common English words and Han text are milder.
Otherwise predict near zero, except at opening quotation marks. These are
strongest after a colon or assignment, weaker in ordinary running prose.
These are broad written-form rules, not a table of token-specific responses.
